{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"in flight drift correction for diversions in flight drift correction for diversions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions.md","fileName":"In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 21:32\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cross-Country Flight Planning and Diversion]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cross-Country Flight Planning and Diversion","Double-Error Drift Correction","Opening-Closing Angle Drift Correction","flightscience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"in flight drift correction for diversions in flight drift correction for diversions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions.md","fileName":"In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions","heading":"In-Flight Drift Correction for Diversions","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A diversion track must be checked against landmarks and elapsed time after the new heading is established. Before halfway, the [[Double-Error Drift Correction]] can return the aircraft to track in the same elapsed time; after halfway, the [[Opening-Closing Angle Drift Correction]] aims directly toward the destination. If the destination bearing is known reliably, direct tracking can replace both approximations.","tags":["baby